  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 17-layer spectrally selective absorber stack on Al substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: Cr | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2. Initialize from round-1 best candidate thicknesses: [69, 188, 218, 229, 100, 67, 240, 184, 151, 135, 226, 195, 232, 199, 222, 78, 119] nm. Constrain layer 4 (SiO2) to 92-108 nm and layer 6 (SiO2) to 232-248 nm. Optimize remaining 14 layer thicknesses with bounds 50-300 nm using gradient_thickness optimizer with reduced step-size. Evaluate absorptance in 400-700 nm and reflectance in 700-2000 nm at normal incidence unpolarized. Score both spectral bands equally. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thicknesses of a 17-layer Cr/HfO2/SiO2 bilayer stack on an aluminum substrate under normal-incidence unpolarized light from air. Use round-1 initialization [69, 188, 218, 229, 100, 67, 240, 184, 151, 135, 226, 195, 232, 199, 222, 78, 119] nm. Constrain the fifth and seventh layers (SiO2) to 92–108 nm and 232–248 nm, respectively. Optimize all layer thicknesses within 50–300 nm to achieve high absorptance and low reflectance in 400–700 nm while maintaining high reflectance and low absorptance in 700–2000 nm, scoring both spectral bands equally.",
